      <section id="scope" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>02</span> Scope of This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>This Privacy Policy applies when you:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>visit or browse our website;</li>
          <li>create or use a customer account;</li>
          <li>add items to your cart or wishlist;</li>
          <li>purchase scarves, bandanas, Indo-Western tops, jewellery or other products;</li>
          <li>make a payment or receive a refund;</li>
          <li>request shipping, delivery, returns, exchanges or after-sales support;</li>
          <li>contact us through email or other communication channels;</li>
          <li>subscribe to newsletters or promotional communications;</li>
          <li>participate in surveys, promotions or customer activities; or</li>
          <li>otherwise interact with Grey Exim online.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="data-we-collect" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>03</span> Personal Data We Collect</h2>
        <p>Depending on how you interact with Grey Exim, we may collect the following categories of personal data.</p>

        <h3>A. Identity and Contact Information</h3>
        <p>This may include:</p>
        <ul class="grey-policy__columns">
          <li>first name;</li><li>last name;</li><li>email address;</li><li>telephone number;</li>
          <li>billing address;</li><li>shipping address;</li><li>city;</li><li>state;</li>
          <li>postal code;</li><li>country; and</li><li>other contact information you voluntarily provide.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>B. Order and Transaction Information</h3>
        <p>This may include:</p>
        <ul class="grey-policy__columns">
          <li>products viewed or purchased;</li><li>product variants, colours, sizes or quantities;</li>
          <li>cart information;</li><li>wishlist information;</li><li>order number;</li><li>purchase date;</li>
          <li>order value;</li><li>discounts or promotional codes used;</li><li>transaction status;</li>
          <li>cancellation information;</li><li>return or exchange information;</li><li>refund status;</li>
          <li>delivery status; and</li><li>previous purchase history.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>C. Delivery Information</h3>
        <p>We may process information necessary to deliver your order, including:</p>
        <ul class="grey-policy__columns">
          <li>recipient name;</li><li>delivery address;</li><li>telephone number;</li><li>delivery instructions;</li>
          <li>shipping status;</li><li>tracking information; and</li><li>other information reasonably necessary for fulfilment and delivery.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>D. Payment-Related Information</h3>
        <p>Payments may be processed through Shopify and/or third-party payment service providers.</p>
        <p>Depending on the payment method used, Grey Exim may receive information such as:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>payment method;</li><li>payment status;</li><li>transaction reference number;</li>
          <li>refund information; and</li><li>limited or masked payment information.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Where complete payment-card credentials, card numbers, CVV or other sensitive payment information are collected directly by a payment gateway or financial service provider, those details are processed through that provider's systems.</p>
        <p>Grey Exim does not represent that it stores complete payment-card credentials unless our actual technical configuration changes to do so.</p>

        <h3>E. Customer Account Information</h3>
        <p>If you create an account, we may process information such as:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>saved contact details;</li><li>saved delivery addresses;</li><li>order history;</li>
          <li>account preferences;</li><li>profile information; and</li><li>account-related activity.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Authentication and account infrastructure may be provided through Shopify or other applicable ecommerce technologies.</p>

        <h3>F. Customer Support and Communication Information</h3>
        <p>If you contact Grey Exim, we may collect information contained in your communication, including information relating to:</p>
        <ul class="grey-policy__columns">
          <li>products;</li><li>orders;</li><li>payments;</li><li>shipping;</li><li>returns;</li>
          <li>refunds;</li><li>complaints;</li><li>account support; and</li><li>general enquiries.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Please do not send unnecessary sensitive, financial or identity information through ordinary email or open-text forms.</p>

        <h3>G. Marketing and Newsletter Information</h3>
        <p>If you voluntarily subscribe to Grey Exim marketing communications, we may process:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your email address;</li><li>subscription status;</li><li>marketing preferences;</li>
          <li>consent records;</li><li>unsubscribe requests; and</li><li>interaction with marketing communications.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>H. Browsing, Device and Usage Information</h3>
        <p>When you visit our website, we and our technology providers may automatically process information such as:</p>
        <ul class="grey-policy__columns">
          <li>IP address;</li><li>browser type;</li><li>device type;</li><li>operating system;</li>
          <li>network information;</li><li>cookie or similar identifiers;</li>
          <li>approximate location derived from technical information;</li><li>pages viewed;</li>
          <li>products viewed;</li><li>referring page;</li><li>cart activity;</li>
          <li>website interactions; and</li><li>date and time of activity.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>I. Security and Fraud-Prevention Information</h3>
        <p>We or our service providers may process relevant account, transaction, device and activity information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>verify transactions;</li><li>protect customer accounts;</li><li>prevent fraud;</li>
          <li>detect suspicious activity;</li><li>prevent misuse;</li><li>investigate security incidents; and</li>
          <li>protect Grey Exim, customers and our systems.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>J. Information You Voluntarily Provide</h3>
        <p>We may process other information you choose to provide when contacting Grey Exim or requesting assistance.</p>
        <p>Please provide only information reasonably relevant to your request.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="collection-methods" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>04</span> How We Collect Personal Data</h2>
        <p>We may collect personal data:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>directly from you when you register, purchase, contact us or subscribe;</li>
          <li>automatically through cookies and similar technologies;</li>
          <li>from Shopify as part of the ecommerce services used by our store;</li>
          <li>from payment providers connected with a transaction;</li>
          <li>from courier and logistics providers;</li>
          <li>from customer-service or technical-service providers;</li>
          <li>from analytics or marketing providers where such services are enabled and permitted; or</li>
          <li>from another person where someone legitimately places an order to be delivered to you.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="how-we-use-data" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>05</span> How We Use Your Personal Data</h2>
        <p>We may use personal data for the following purposes.</p>

        <h3>A. To Operate Our Online Store</h3>
        <p>We use information to:</p>
        <ul><li>maintain our website;</li><li>provide ecommerce functionality;</li><li>operate customer accounts;</li><li>maintain shopping carts;</li><li>maintain wishlists;</li><li>remember preferences; and</li><li>provide services requested by customers.</li></ul>

        <h3>B. To Process and Fulfil Orders</h3>
        <p>We use information to:</p>
        <ul><li>verify and administer orders;</li><li>confirm payment;</li><li>prepare products;</li><li>issue confirmations or invoices;</li><li>arrange fulfilment;</li><li>deliver orders; and</li><li>communicate order updates.</li></ul>

        <h3>C. To Provide Shipping and Tracking</h3>
        <p>We use delivery information to:</p>
        <ul><li>generate shipping documentation;</li><li>arrange delivery;</li><li>provide tracking;</li><li>resolve delivery issues; and</li><li>manage return shipments.</li></ul>

        <h3>D. To Process Cancellations, Returns, Exchanges and Refunds</h3>
        <p>We may use order, payment, delivery and communication information to:</p>
        <ul><li>determine eligibility;</li><li>arrange return collection;</li><li>provide replacement products;</li><li>process refunds; and</li><li>maintain transaction records.</li></ul>

        <h3>E. To Maintain Customer Accounts</h3>
        <p>Where you create an account, we may use relevant information to:</p>
        <ul><li>administer your account;</li><li>display orders;</li><li>maintain saved details;</li><li>manage preferences; and</li><li>provide account support.</li></ul>

        <h3>F. To Provide Customer Support</h3>
        <p>We may use information to respond to:</p>
        <ul><li>product enquiries;</li><li>order enquiries;</li><li>shipping issues;</li><li>payment concerns;</li><li>returns;</li><li>refunds;</li><li>complaints; and</li><li>other customer requests.</li></ul>

        <h3>G. To Send Transactional and Service Communications</h3>
        <p>We may send communications relating to:</p>
        <ul class="grey-policy__columns"><li>order confirmation;</li><li>payment confirmation;</li><li>shipping;</li><li>delivery;</li><li>tracking;</li><li>returns;</li><li>refunds;</li><li>account security;</li><li>customer support; and</li><li>other necessary service-related matters.</li></ul>
        <p>These communications are different from optional promotional marketing.</p>

        <h3>H. To Send Marketing Communications</h3>
        <p>Where you have subscribed, consented, or where otherwise permitted under applicable law, we may send information about:</p>
        <ul class="grey-policy__columns"><li>new products;</li><li>scarves;</li><li>bandanas;</li><li>Indo-Western tops;</li><li>jewellery;</li><li>new arrivals;</li><li>promotions;</li><li>discounts;</li><li>offers; and</li><li>other Grey Exim updates.</li></ul>
        <p>You may unsubscribe at any time using the unsubscribe option in the communication or by contacting us.</p>
        <p>Withdrawing from marketing does not prevent us from sending necessary transactional or customer-service messages.</p>

        <h3>I. To Improve Our Website and Customer Experience</h3>
        <p>We may use information to:</p>
        <ul><li>understand website usage;</li><li>evaluate website performance;</li><li>improve navigation;</li><li>improve merchandising;</li><li>improve products and services;</li><li>diagnose technical issues; and</li><li>understand customer interest in product categories.</li></ul>

        <h3>J. To Personalise the Shopping Experience</h3>
        <p>Where permitted, we may use browsing or transaction information to:</p>
        <ul><li>remember preferences;</li><li>display relevant products;</li><li>customise website content; or</li><li>make product recommendations.</li></ul>

        <h3>K. For Security and Fraud Prevention</h3>
        <p>We may process information to:</p>
        <ul><li>protect customer accounts;</li><li>protect transactions;</li><li>identify suspicious activity;</li><li>prevent unlawful use;</li><li>prevent fraud; and</li><li>safeguard our systems.</li></ul>

        <h3>L. To Comply With Legal and Regulatory Requirements</h3>
        <p>We may retain or process information where reasonably necessary to:</p>
        <ul><li>comply with tax requirements;</li><li>maintain accounting records;</li><li>comply with applicable laws;</li><li>respond to lawful requests;</li><li>establish or defend legal claims;</li><li>enforce contractual rights; or</li><li>protect legal rights and safety.</li></ul>
      </section>

      <section id="consent" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>06</span> Consent and Your Choices</h2>
        <p>Where Grey Exim relies on consent, we aim to obtain consent through a clear and affirmative action for a specified purpose.</p>
        <p>You are not required to consent to promotional marketing in order to purchase a product from Grey Exim.</p>
        <p>Certain information may be necessary to complete an order. If you do not provide required information, we may be unable to:</p>
        <ul><li>process your order;</li><li>arrange payment;</li><li>deliver your products; or</li><li>provide the requested service.</li></ul>
        <p>Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw that consent through the mechanism provided or by contacting Grey Exim.</p>
        <p>Withdrawal of consent does not invalidate processing lawfully carried out before withdrawal and does not necessarily require deletion of information that we are required or permitted to retain under applicable law.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>07</span> Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
        <p>Grey Exim and our technology providers may use:</p>
        <ul><li>cookies;</li><li>pixels;</li><li>tags;</li><li>local storage; and</li><li>similar technologies.</li></ul>
        <p>These technologies may be used to:</p>
        <ul><li>operate our website;</li><li>maintain shopping carts;</li><li>remember preferences;</li><li>secure the website;</li><li>measure website performance;</li><li>conduct analytics; and</li><li>where enabled and permitted, support marketing or advertising.</li></ul>
        <p>Because our website is powered by Shopify, Shopify-related technologies may also place cookies or similar technologies on the website.</p>
        <p>Additional information about cookies and tracking technologies should be provided in our Cookie Policy and, where applicable, through cookie-preference controls.</p>
        <p>Where applicable law requires consent before non-essential analytics, advertising or similar technologies are used, appropriate choices will be provided.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>08</span> How We Share Personal Data</h2>
        <p>We may share personal data only where reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.</p>

        <h3>A. Shopify</h3>
        <p>Our online store is powered by Shopify.</p>
        <p>Information necessary to operate our ecommerce store may be transmitted to and processed by Shopify in connection with services such as:</p>
        <ul><li>storefront functionality;</li><li>checkout;</li><li>customer accounts;</li><li>carts;</li><li>transaction processing support;</li><li>website infrastructure; and</li><li>related ecommerce services.</li></ul>
        <p>Depending on the Shopify features enabled by Grey Exim, certain Shopify services may involve additional processing under Shopify's own privacy terms.</p>

        <h3>B. Payment and Financial Service Providers</h3>
        <p>We may share information necessary to complete or verify transactions with:</p>
        <ul><li>payment gateways;</li><li>banks;</li><li>card networks;</li><li>payment networks; and</li><li>other payment service providers.</li></ul>

        <h3>C. Courier, Fulfilment and Logistics Providers</h3>
        <p>We may share information such as:</p>
        <ul><li>recipient name;</li><li>delivery address;</li><li>phone number;</li><li>order information; and</li><li>delivery instructions</li></ul>
        <p>with courier and logistics providers where required to deliver, track or return an order.</p>

        <h3>D. Technology and Service Providers</h3>
        <p>We may use providers for services such as:</p>
        <ul><li>hosting;</li><li>ecommerce infrastructure;</li><li>cloud services;</li><li>customer support;</li><li>technical maintenance;</li><li>email services;</li><li>website functionality;</li><li>fraud prevention; and</li><li>security.</li></ul>

        <h3>E. Analytics, Advertising and Marketing Providers</h3>
        <p>Where relevant services are enabled and permitted under applicable law, usage, cookie or advertising-related information may be processed by analytics, advertising or marketing providers.</p>

        <h3>F. Professional Advisers</h3>
        <p>We may disclose relevant information to:</p>
        <ul><li>accountants;</li><li>auditors;</li><li>legal advisers;</li><li>insurers; and</li><li>other professional advisers</li></ul>
        <p>where reasonably necessary.</p>

        <h3>G. Government Authorities and Legal Recipients</h3>
        <p>We may disclose personal data where required by:</p>
        <ul><li>applicable law;</li><li>lawful governmental request;</li><li>court order;</li><li>legal process; or</li><li>regulatory requirement.</li></ul>
        <p>We may also disclose information where reasonably necessary to protect rights, safety or security.</p>

        <h3>H. Corporate Transactions</h3>
        <p>If Grey Exim is involved in a:</p>
        <ul><li>merger;</li><li>acquisition;</li><li>restructuring;</li><li>financing;</li><li>transfer;</li><li>sale of business; or</li><li>sale of assets,</li></ul>
        <p>relevant personal data may be disclosed or transferred as permitted under applicable law.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="shopify-services" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>09</span> Shopify Enhanced Services and Related Features</h2>
        <p>Grey Exim may use Shopify features that involve processing information to improve ecommerce functionality, analytics, personalisation, security or related services.</p>
        <p>Where a Shopify feature requires additional disclosure, customer choice or consent, Grey Exim will provide the required information and controls as applicable.</p>
        <p>Shopify settings and services may change from time to time, and Grey Exim may update this Privacy Policy accordingly.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>10</span> Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We retain personal data only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected or for another period required or permitted under applicable law.</p>
        <p>Retention periods may depend on factors including:</p>
        <ul><li>whether an order remains active;</li><li>whether you maintain a customer account;</li><li>whether information is needed for shipping;</li><li>whether information is needed for returns or refunds;</li><li>whether customer support remains active;</li><li>legal or accounting obligations;</li><li>tax requirements;</li><li>security and fraud prevention;</li><li>disputes or legal claims; and</li><li>active marketing subscriptions.</li></ul>
        <p>Where personal data is no longer required for a lawful purpose, we will take reasonable steps to delete, anonymise or otherwise appropriately dispose of it, subject to applicable legal, backup and record-retention requirements.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="security" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>11</span> Data Security</h2>
        <p>Grey Exim uses reasonable administrative, technical and organisational safeguards appropriate to the nature of the personal data and the risks involved.</p>
        <p>These measures are intended to protect personal data against:</p>
        <ul><li>unauthorised access;</li><li>unauthorised use;</li><li>disclosure;</li><li>alteration;</li><li>loss;</li><li>theft; and</li><li>destruction.</li></ul>
        <p>We also rely on technology providers and payment providers to maintain security controls appropriate to the systems they operate.</p>
        <p>However, no internet transmission, website, storage system or security measure can guarantee absolute security.</p>
        <p>Customers should avoid sharing highly sensitive information through ordinary or unsecured communication channels unless necessary.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="breaches" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>12</span> Personal Data Breaches</h2>
        <p>If Grey Exim becomes aware of a personal data breach, we may:</p>
        <ul><li>investigate the incident;</li><li>take reasonable steps to contain it;</li><li>mitigate potential harm;</li><li>secure affected systems; and</li><li>notify affected individuals or competent authorities where and when required under applicable law.</li></ul>
      </section>

      <section id="children" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>13</span> Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>For the purposes of applicable Indian data-protection requirements, a child may include an individual below 18 years of age.</p>
        <p>Grey Exim's ecommerce services are not designed for children to independently provide personal data where applicable law requires parental or guardian involvement.</p>
        <p>Where required by applicable law, Grey Exim may require verifiable consent from a parent or lawful guardian before processing a child's personal data.</p>
        <p>Grey Exim does not intend to engage in prohibited tracking, behavioural monitoring or targeted advertising directed at children.</p>
        <p>If you are a parent or lawful guardian and believe a child has provided personal data contrary to applicable requirements, please contact: <a href="mailto:care@greyexim.com">care@greyexim.com</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>14</span> Your Privacy Rights</h2>
        <p>Subject to applicable law, circumstances and legal exceptions, you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul><li>obtain information about personal data being processed;</li><li>request correction of inaccurate information;</li><li>request completion of incomplete information;</li><li>request updating of personal information;</li><li>request erasure where retention is no longer required or permitted;</li><li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent;</li><li>raise a grievance regarding our handling of personal data; and</li><li>exercise nomination rights where such rights are applicable.</li></ul>
        <p>Additional rights may be available depending on the laws of the jurisdiction applicable to you.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="exercise-rights" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>15</span> How to Exercise Your Privacy Rights</h2>
        <p>To submit a privacy request, please contact:</p>
        <div class="grey-policy__callout">
          <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:care@greyexim.com?subject=Privacy%20Request">care@greyexim.com</a><br><strong>Subject:</strong> Privacy Request</p>
        </div>
        <p>Please provide sufficient information for Grey Exim to:</p>
        <ul><li>understand your request;</li><li>identify the relevant customer record; and</li><li>verify your identity where appropriate.</li></ul>
        <p>We may take reasonable steps to verify that a requester is the relevant individual or is lawfully authorised to act on that person's behalf.</p>
        <p>We will respond within the period required by applicable law.</p>
        <p>Certain information may not be deleted immediately where retention remains necessary to:</p>
        <ul><li>fulfil an order;</li><li>meet accounting requirements;</li><li>meet tax requirements;</li><li>investigate fraud;</li><li>resolve a dispute;</li><li>comply with law; or</li><li>exercise or defend legal rights.</li></ul>
      </section>

      <section id="marketing" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>16</span> Marketing Preferences</h2>
        <p>You may opt out of promotional emails by:</p>
        <ul><li>using the unsubscribe option in the communication; or</li><li>contacting Grey Exim.</li></ul>
        <p>Unsubscribing from marketing does not normally affect communications relating to:</p>
        <ul><li>orders;</li><li>payments;</li><li>shipping;</li><li>deliveries;</li><li>returns;</li><li>refunds;</li><li>account security; or</li><li>customer-support requests.</li></ul>
      </section>

      <section id="international" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>17</span> International Processing and Transfers</h2>
        <p>Grey Exim uses ecommerce, cloud, technology and service providers that may operate internationally.</p>
        <p>Accordingly, personal data may in some circumstances be processed outside India.</p>
        <p>Where applicable, Grey Exim will comply with Indian requirements concerning cross-border processing and any restrictions or requirements imposed by competent authorities.</p>
        <p>Where customers are protected by additional privacy laws in another jurisdiction, legally applicable safeguards will be applied as required.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="third-parties" class="grey-policy__section">
        <h2><span>18</span> Third-Party Websites and Services</h2>
        <p>Our website may contain links, integrations or services operated by third parties.</p>
        <p>When you leave Grey Exim's website or interact directly with an independent third-party service, that third party may process your personal data under its own privacy practices.</p>
        <p>Grey Exim does not control independent third-party websites or services and encourages you to review the relevant third party's privacy policy before providing personal information.</p>
